{"book":9,"chapter":9,"context":{"chapter":9,"title":"Searching for Lost Donkeys","summary":"Saul, a tall young Benjamite, goes looking for his father's lost donkeys and on his servant's advice seeks out the seer Samuel. God had already told Samuel to expect the man who would lead Israel, and Samuel honors Saul at a sacrificial meal.","background":"A note explains that a prophet used to be called a 'seer' (v. 9), showing the book was written for later readers. Before the temple, worship took place at local 'high places' on hilltops (v. 12). Benjamin was the smallest tribe, nearly wiped out in Judges 20, which is why Saul protests his low standing (v. 21).","customs":[{"term":"Fourth part of a shekel","verses":"9:7-8","note":"Visitors customarily brought a gift when consulting a prophet. A quarter shekel was a small piece of silver."},{"term":"The shoulder","verses":"9:23-24","note":"A choice portion of the sacrifice, set aside for the guest of honor."}],"watchFor":["Lost donkeys become the means of God's plan (vv. 3, 15–16).","'Captain over my people' (v. 16): a leader appointed under God.","'Am not I a Benjamite, of the smallest of the tribes?' (v. 21)."],"connections":["Judges 20:46-48","Deuteronomy 17:15","1 Kings 14:3","Acts 13:21"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi-","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he was"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsa","a man"],["מִבִּנְיָמִין","mibinyamin","H1144","HR/Npm","from Benjamin"],["","[ ]","","","[ ]"],["וּשְׁמוֹ","ushemo","H8034","HC/Ncmsc/Sp3ms","and name his"],["קִישׁ","kish","H7027","HNpm","[was] Kish"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אֲבִיאֵל","'avi'el","H22","HNpm","Abiel"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["צְרוֹר","tzeror","H6872","HNpm","Zeror"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["בְּכוֹרַת","bekhorat","H1064","HNpm","Becorath"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אֲפִיחַ","'afiach","H647","HNpm","Aphiah"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","a son of"],["אִישׁ","'ish