"verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[1,16,21]},{"id":"kish_1784","name":"Kish","also":"Cis","summary":"A Benjamite, the son of Abiel, and father of king Saul (1 Sam. 9:1, 3; 10:11, 21; 14:51; 2 Sam. 21:14). All that is recorded of him is that he sent his son Saul in search of his asses that had strayed, and that he was buried in Zelah.","verses":13,"father":"Abiel","mother":"Maachah","v":[1,3]},{"id":"abiel_23","name":"Abiel","also":"Ner, Jehiel","summary":"The son of Zeror and father of Ner, who was the grandfather of Saul (1 Sam. 14:51; 1 Chr. 8:33; 9:39).","verses":5,"father":"Zeror","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"aphiah_274","name":"Aphiah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"bechorath_425","name":"Bechorath","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Aphiah","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"zeror_3052","name":"Zeror","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Bechorath","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2]},{"id":"saul_2478","name":"Saul","also":"","summary":"The son of Kish (probably his only son, and a child of prayer, “asked for”), of the tribe of Benjamin, the first king of the Jewish nation. The singular providential circumstances connected with his election as king are recorded in 1 Sam. 8-10.","verses":265,"father":"Kish","mother":"","v":[2,3,5,7,8,10,15,17,18,19,21,22,24,25,26,27]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[4]},{"id":"samuel_2469","name":"Samuel","also":"Shemuel","summary":"Heard of God. The peculiar circumstances connected with his birth are recorded in 1 Sam. 1:20. Hannah, one of the two wives of Elkanah, who came up to Shiloh to worship before the Lord, earnestly prayed to God that she might become the mother of a son.","verses":122,"father":"Elkanah","mother":"Hannah","v":[14,15,17,18,19,22,23,24,25,26,27]}],"places":[{"id":"shaalim_1054","name":"Shaalim","kind":"","lat":31.84685,"lon":35.18491,"summary":"Land of foxes, a place apparently to the north-west of Jerusalem (1 Sam. 9:4), perhaps in the neighbourhood of Shaalabbin in Dan (Josh. 19:42).","verses":1,"v":[4]},{"id":"shalishah_1058","name":"Shalishah","kind":"","lat":31.84685,"lon":35.18491,"summary":"Probably the district of Baal-shalisha (2 Kings 4:42), lying about 12 miles north of Lydda (1 Sam. 9:4).","verses":1,"v":[4]},{"id":"zuph_1276","name":"Zuph","kind":"Region","lat":31.84685,"lon":35.18491,"summary":"(1 Sam. 9:5, 6), a district in which lay Samuel’s city, Ramah.","verses":1,"v":[5]}],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_saul_150","title":"Birth of Saul","year":-1135,"summary":"Passage: 1 Samuel 9:2. People: Saul.","v":[2]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1961,1961,1961,1144,1144,1368,1368,1368,8034,8034,7027,7027,1121,22,22,1121,1121,6872,6872,1121,1121,1064,1064,1121,1121,647,647,3227,3227],[0,1961,1961,1121,1121,8034,7586,970,2896,2896,369,369,4480,1121,1121,7926,1364,3605,3605,5971,5971,5971],[860,860,860,860,7586,7586,1,7027,6,6,7027,7027,559,413,1121,1121,7586,3947,259,5288,5288,5288,1980,1980,1245,1245,860,860],[5674,5674,5674,2022,2022,2022,2022,669,669,776,776,776,776,776,8031,8031,3808,3808,3808,3808,4672,4672,4672,5674,5674,5674,5674,5674,776,776,776,8171,8171,369,369,369,369,369,5674,5674,5674,776,776,776,3227,3227,3808,3808,3808,3808,3808,4672,4672],[1992,1992,935,776,776,6689,6689,7586,559,5288,5288,5288,1980,7725,7725,7725,7725,6435,1,1,2308,2308,2308,4480,860,860,1672,1672,1672,0,